title Which edits re-run the archive check
base src/

== graph Archive triggers
ranks: Who acts | Event | Gate | Result
-- Who acts
draft: Editor saves a draft [actor] @docs/save.ts:40 # autosave
approve: Reviewer approves [actor] @review/approve.ts:18
title_edit: Editor renames the doc [actor] @docs/edit.ts:33
*retag: Librarian re-tags [actor] @docs/tags.ts:9 # shelf · owner · labels
-- Event
saved: DocSaved [event] @events/doc.ts:12 # kind = DRAFT
approved: DocSaved [event] @events/doc.ts:12 # kind = APPROVED
updated: DocUpdated [event] @events/doc.ts:20 # fields = […]
-- Gate
onsave: Save handler [gate] @archive/handlers.ts:22 # passes APPROVED only
onupdate: Update handler [gate] @archive/handlers.ts:41 # passes title, shelf, labels
-- Result
check: Archive check [result] @archive/run.ts:7 # new ArchiveRun
  writes: ArchiveRun
skip: Ignored [result] # no new check

autosave: draft > saved > onsave =| skip | DRAFT | Autosaves reach the save handler, which drops anything not APPROVED.
approval: approve > approved > onsave => check | APPROVED | Approval is the only save that starts a check.
rename: title_edit > updated > onupdate => check
shelf: retag > updated > onupdate => check
owner: retag > updated > onupdate =| skip | owner | A re-tag that only changes owner is dropped at the gate: nothing re-checks owner.

== cover What the check reads, and what keeps it fresh
title: re-checks on rename <- rename
body: set at approval <- approval
shelf: re-checks on change <- shelf
owner: changes don't re-check <- owner
?labels: triggers, not read yet
